  speakerName: VENDOR IRAH
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: '"Sometimes a simple thank you isn''t enough to express how grateful
    you feel.

    In Ilokano, ''agyamanak unay'' means ''thank you very much.''

    You
    can use it when someone does something especially kind or generous for you.

    Listen
    carefully: agyamanak unay.

    Now, try saying ''agyamanak unay'' yourself."

'
